Measured while landing objectui#8513 (`ValueDataSource`'s object-dialect combinators). Out of that card's scope — different package, different defect shape, different fix — so it is filed rather than folded in. ⛔ Not claimed.

## The mismatch

`packages/plugin-gantt/src/ObjectGantt.tsx`, inside `reload`:

```ts
if (hasInlineData && dataProvider === 'value') {
  if (isCurrent()) {
    setData(dataItems as any[]);
    setRowCeiling({ truncated: false });
  }
  return;
}
```

It returns BEFORE the `effectiveDataSource.find(...)` call a dozen lines below — the call that is the only place `schema.filter`, `schema.sort` and the `NON_GRID_ROW_CEILING_TOP` ceiling are applied. So on a `provider: 'value'` gantt:

- an authored `filter` reaches nothing and **every** inline row is charted;
- an authored `sort` reaches nothing;
- `applyNonGridRowCeiling` never runs, so the objectui#7210 ceiling is not enforced on this provider.

The adapter it skips is `ValueDataSource`, which implements `$filter`, `$orderby`, `$skip`, `$top` and `$select` locally — so the short-circuit is not working around a missing capability. `resolveDataSource` already returns exactly that adapter for this provider, four lines away.

## Failure direction

**Fail-OPEN.** A gantt that declares a filter draws the rows it declared it would hide. That is the opposite direction from objectui#8513 (which returned no rows) and the same direction objectui#8447 was filed about — worth stating because the two are easy to fold together and must not be.

## Why it is not a scope question

objectui#8220 is nearby but different: it says three plugin REGISTRATIONS declare neither `filter` nor `sort` while the renderers lower both onto the query. This card is about the one provider where the renderer does not reach the query at all. objectui#7333 is also nearby and also different — it is the OTHER short-circuit in the same function (the host-`data` one firing on an empty array).

## Suggested shape, not a ruling

The inline branch could seed `setData` from `ValueDataSource` with the same query params the object/api branch builds, rather than from `dataItems` raw. Whether the ceiling should apply to an inline array at all is a real question and is why this is filed rather than fixed in passing.

## Dedup

Run, and the instrument was validated in the same session with a control query that returned a known-present card. `search_issues` (repo-scoped, semantic): the gantt/filter/sort neighbourhood returns objectui#8174, #8220, #7237, #7333, #7334 and objectui#8513 — 18 total, none of them this. Closed cards were in range (the same session's control returned closed objectui#8447 / #8515 / #8600).


